---
import ProductLayout from "../layouts/ProductLayout.astro";

const description = "Nostekon's roadmap: what already works, and the work needed to make one isolated restore drill trustworthy end to end.";

const phases = [
  { title: "Rehearse real backup files", state: "Done, early", later: false, items: ["PostgreSQL custom archives restored on a local isolated Docker target", "No production connection, credentials, ports or writable host mounts", "Reviewable plans bind exact backup bytes, cached image ID and expectations", "Bound V4 profiles check nulls, uniqueness and references with read-only queries", "Changed backups and plan-setting overrides rejected before execution", "Cleanup, failure evidence and independent Go/Studio report evaluation", "Private locked checkpoints and confirmed exact-target hard-stop cleanup", "Next gate: an approved sanitized production-origin backup pilot"] },
  { title: "Define the drill", state: "Done", later: false, items: ["Versioned YAML drill contract", "Scenario templates and the interactive Studio", "Strict validation in the Go API"] },
  { title: "Evaluate recorded evidence", state: "Done, early", later: false, items: ["V0 to V4 verdicts with the first failed level", "Recovery time by phase, including unaccounted time", "Exact data loss from an acknowledged-write ledger", "Studio report review and export", "Local and optional server-side signed-evidence verification", "Prometheus metrics and a bundled Grafana dashboard"] },
  { title: "Run isolated policy suites", state: "Done, lab only", later: false, items: ["Separate source and restore k3d clusters", "Delete the source namespace after backup", "Bounded PostgreSQL writes with a durable host ledger", "V3 row count and validated V4 restored IDs", "Zero-loss, strict tail-loss and budgeted-loss cases", "Atomic summaries and partial capture retention", "Independent Go CLI suite gate and Studio review export", "Clean up namespaces"] },
  { title: "Keep a usable local workspace", state: "Done, early", later: false, items: ["Hardened same-origin Docker app; execution off by default", "Explicit host opt-in, bounded jobs, cancellation and recovery confirmation", "Manifest-verified portable host-job evidence bundles", "Atomic case saving and original-evidence export", "Bounded suite history with fresh re-evaluation and independent deletion", "Public-key fingerprint confirmation, local trust/revocation and exact signed exports", "Signed-archive round-trip with fresh checks and no automatic trust", "Shared Go signature verification in the browser and installed API", "Desktop and mobile browser regressions; hosted CI validation remains next"] },
  { title: "Harden execution and capture", state: "Next", later: true, items: ["Map signing keys to operator identity and define organization-wide rotation/revocation", "Instrument live application acknowledgements and independently attest capture", "Owner-validated business-rule coverage beyond basic semantic profiles", "Validate hosted CI lab runs and staging interruption recovery", "More scenarios, and guidance for operating this safely"] },
];
---
<ProductLayout title="Roadmap" description={description} current="roadmap">
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Make one drill trustworthy end to end</h1>
      <p class="lead">Real PostgreSQL backup files can now be rehearsed locally without contacting production. The next gate is a controlled production-origin backup pilot, then approved backup access, application checks and independently measured data loss.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="rows">
      {phases.map((phase) => (
        <div class="row">
          <h2>{phase.title}</h2>
          <ul>
            {phase.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <span class:list={["row-state", { later: phase.later }]}>{phase.state}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="margin-top: 48px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Staying small on purpose</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Restore orchestration touches clusters, storage and application data, so the first version is deliberately narrow: one supported stack, one separate restore cluster, one scenario, a bounded run time and explicit cleanup.</p>
        <p>Production-origin backups stay on isolated restore targets. Direct production connections, failure injection and in-place restores remain unsupported. <a class="link" href="/docs/guides/postgresql-backup-rehearsal/">Backup rehearsal guide and readiness gates</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>
